<BaseLayout title="RPG · David Silva" description="A home for the worldbuilding and behind-the-scenes of my tabletop campaign, Filhos da Tormenta.">
  <h1>RPG</h1>

  <p>
    This is where I bring the tabletop side of my work into a place that can
    hold it. I run a campaign called <strong>Filhos da Tormenta</strong>, started
    in 2025 and still going, with an ending planned for around 2028. For two years
    now I have been writing its world, its characters, and the threads that tie
    them together, and most of that has lived in scattered notes. This section is
    the effort to give it a proper home.
  </p>

  <p>
    We play <strong>Tormenta 20</strong>, the system published by
    <strong>Jambô Editora</strong>, a Brazilian studio. I also have a long-standing
    soft spot for <strong>Vampire: The Masquerade</strong>, and some of what shows
    up here will lean on that love for a darker, character-first kind of story.
  </p>

  <p>
    I keep saying, on this site and off it, that the work I enjoy is turning
    complexity into something another person can pick up and use. A campaign is
    exactly that problem in another form, so expect the same instinct here: notes
    made legible, decisions explained, a world you could step into.
  </p>

  <h2>What is coming here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The world.</strong> Places, factions, and the lore behind Filhos da Tormenta.</li>
    <li><strong>Sessions.</strong> Recaps and the loose threads still in play.</li>
    <li><strong>Behind the screen.</strong> How I build encounters, pace an arc, and keep a long campaign coherent.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="soon">Nothing published yet. The first entries are on their way.</p>
</BaseLayout>

